---
{
  title: "each_async"
}
---
### NAME

    each_async() - Executes a function for each element in an array or
    mapping, yielding to the event loop between elements.

### SYNOPSIS

    async varargs void each_async( mixed src, function fun, mixed extra... );

### DESCRIPTION

    Executes a function for each element in an array or mapping, yielding to
    the event loop between elements.

    The async counterpart to each(). Dispatch is identical — arrays call the
    function with (element, index, array, ...extra), mappings with (key,
    value, mapping, ...extra) — but every call is preceded by an await
    async_yield(), so the driver reads input, queues commands and fires
    timers between elements, and each iteration resumes with a fresh
    evaluation-cost budget. That makes this the shape for walking a
    collection too large to process in one pass.

    The callback is awaited, so an async callback runs to completion before
    the next element begins.

    The iteration rejects with ASYNC_ERR_OWNER_GONE if the object owning the
    callback is destructed while this is parked. That frame lives in the
    simul_efun object, which outlives every caller, so without the check it
    would wake up and call a function pointer with a dead owner — a hard
    error raised here, naming an object that no longer exists. The check is
    per element rather than only on entry, because the owner can go away
    during any yield.

    It rejects rather than returning quietly because the callback's owner
    and the awaiter need not be the same object: `await each_async(src, f)`
    where `f` belongs to something else leaves a caller still waiting for an
    answer, and fulfilling would tell it the collection was walked when it
    was not. Where the two *are* the same object — the common case — there
    is nobody left to hear it, and the rejection costs one debug-log line
    and no traceback.

    Await it from inside an async function. Argument errors reject the
    returned promise rather than throwing at the call site, so a caller that
    discards the promise learns nothing about them.

### PARAMETERS

    src    (mixed)
           Array or mapping to iterate over

    fun    (function)
           Function called per element/pair (see above)

    extra  (mixed, optional)
           Additional arguments passed to the callback starting at $4

### ERRORS

    If src is not an array or mapping, or fun is not a valid function.
    Either rejects the returned promise. ASYNC_ERR_OWNER_GONE if the
    callback's owner is destructed while the iteration is parked.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}await each_async(keys(rooms), (: index_room($1) :));{{di0}}
